{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Giant_Head","to":"Giant Head"},{"from":"Bronze_Automaton","to":"Bronze Automaton"},{"from":"The_Collector","to":"The Collector"},{"from":"Shelled_Parasite","to":"Shelled Parasite"},{"from":"Jaw_Worm","to":"Jaw Worm"},{"from":"Slime_Boss","to":"Slime Boss"},{"from":"Gremlin_Leader","to":"Gremlin Leader"},{"from":"Awakened_One","to":"Awakened One"},{"from":"Spire_Growth","to":"Spire Growth"},{"from":"Gremlin_Nob","to":"Gremlin Nob"}],"pages":{"3028":{"pageid":3028,"ns":0,"title":"Awakened One","revisions":[{"revid":56887,"parentid":56028,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Awakened One\n|Image  = AwakenedOne.png\n|Icon   = Map-Awakened.png\n|HP     = 300\n|AscHP  = 320\n|Powers = {{BD|Regenerate}} 10 ({{Asc|19|15}}) <br> {{BD|Curiosity}} 1 ({{Asc|19|2}}) <br> ({{BD|Strength}} 2 {{Asc|4}})\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Boss\n}} {{Power Infobox|Curiosity}} {{Power Infobox|Regenerate}} {{Power Infobox|Unawakened}}\nThe Awakened One is a [[Boss]] found at the end of [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Awakened One\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Slash\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals 20 damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Soul Strike\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals 6\u00d74 damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Rebirth\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Heals to full HP. Removes all [[Debuffs]]. Loses {{BD|Curiosity}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Curiosity\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Dark Echo\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals 40 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Sludge\n|Intent = DebuffAttack4\n|Effect = Deals 18 damage. Adds a {{C|Void}} into your draw pile.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals 10\u00d73 damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n=== Phase One ===\nAlways starts with {{Int|Awakened One|Slash}}.\n\n'''Every turn after:'''\n* {{Int|Awakened One|Soul Strike}} 25% chance\n* {{Int|Awakened One|Slash}} 75% chance\n\n{{Int|Awakened One|Slash}} cannot be used three times in a row. {{Int|Awakened One|Soul Strike}} cannot be used twice in a row.\n\n=== Phase Two ===\nOnce its HP reaches 0, it loses {{BD|Curiosity}} and its intent changes to {{Int|Awakened One|Rebirth}}. Any {{BD|Strength}} gained from {{BD|Curiosity}} is kept.\n\nAlways starts Phase Two with {{Int|Awakened One|Dark Echo}}. Afterward, it has a 50/50 chance to use {{Int|Awakened One|Tackle}} or {{Int|Awakened One|Sludge}}. It cannot use either of these moves three times in a row.\n\nThe remaining {{M|Cultist|Cultists}} will flee when the Awakened One is defeated in Phase Two.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The {{M|Cultist|Cultists}} in this fight are not {{BD|Minion|Minions}} despite fleeing when the Awakened One is defeated so {{KW|Fatal}} effects will still trigger when killing them.\n* {{R|Matryoshka}} and {{R|Eternal Feather}} both reference this boss in their flavor text.\n* According to {{R|Bird-Faced Urn|Bird-Faced Urn's}} flavor text, the Awakened One is the crow god Mazaleth.\n** Fittingly, the {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}} has an effect triggered by playing {{QueryLink|Cards|type:power|Power}} cards, just like the Awakened One's {{BD|Curiosity}}.\n* A {{C|Ritual Dagger}} is stuck in its chest.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"2429":{"pageid":2429,"ns":0,"title":"Bronze Automaton","revisions":[{"revid":56914,"parentid":56913,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Ambox\n| title = WARNING!\n| color = red\n| icon = GremlinNob.png\n| message = ''This page is under construction. Information may be wrong or incomplete.''\n}}\n\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Bronze Automaton\n|Image  = BronzeAutomaton.png\n|Icon   = Map-Automaton.png\n|HP     = 300\n|AscHP  = 320\n|Powers = {{BD|Artifact}} 3\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Boss\n}}\n'''Bronze Automaton''' is a [[Boss]] found at the end of [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Bronze Automaton}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Spawn Orbs\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Summons 2 {{M|Bronze Orb|Bronze Orbs}}.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Flail\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (7\u00d72;{{Asc|4|8x2}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Boost\n|Intent = DefendBuff\n|Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|4|4}}) {{BD|Strength}} and (9;{{Asc|9|12}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Strength, Block\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = HYPER BEAM\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (45;{{Asc|4|50}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stunned\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Does nothing.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways starts with {{Int|Bronze Automaton|Spawn Orbs}}, then repeats the following pattern:\n#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Flail}}\n#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Boost}}\n#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Flail}}\n#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Boost}}\n#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|HYPER BEAM}}\n#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Stunned}}\n\nOn {{Asc|19|Ascension}}, '''Bronze Automaton''' will always use {{Int|Bronze Automaton|Boost}} in place of {{Int|Bronze Automaton|Stunned}}.\n\n= Bronze Orb =\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Bronze Orb\n|Image  = BronzeOrb.png\n|HP     = 52-58\n|AscHP  = 54-60\n|Powers = {{BD|Minion}}\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Minion\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Stasis}}\n'''Bronze Orb''' is a {{BD|Minion}} summoned only by the {{M|Bronze Automaton}}.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Bronze Orb}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stasis\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = {{BD|Stasis|Steals}} a random card of the highest rarity from your draw pile (or discard pile, if the draw pile is empty). On death, returns the card to your hand.\n|GivesToEnemy = Stasis\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Support Beam\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = {{M|Bronze Automaton}} gains 12 {{KW|Block}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Block\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Beam\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals 8 damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nEach '''Bronze Orb''' can only use {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} once per combat. {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} has a 75% chance to be used each turn until it has been picked. After using {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} '''Bronze Orb''' has a 70% chance to use {{Int|Bronze Orb|Support Beam}} and a 30% chance to use {{Int|Bronze Orb|Beam}} each turn. '''Bronze Orb''' cannot use the same attack thrice in a row.\n=== Stasis ===\n{{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} will always prioritize the highest [[Cards#Card Rarity|rarity]] Card in your draw pile. If your draw pile is empty, {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} will pick from your discard pile instead. Cards in {{BD|Stasis}} will not be affected by certain variables; for example, {{C|Masterful Stab}}'s {{KW|Energy}} cost will not increase even if the player takes damage.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n= Hints =\n\n= Trivia =\n* '''Bronze Automaton's''' {{Int|Bronze Automaton|HYPER BEAM}} attack is a reference to the [https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Hyper_Beam_(move) move of the same name] from the ''Pok\u00e9mon'' series.\n\n= Update History =\n* Patch V2.0: The Watcher\n** Stasis move from Bronze Automaton's Orbs is now seeded.\n\n* Patch V1.1: The Dealer\n** Fixed Automaton's orbs preventing scaling of Genetic Algorithm and Ritual Dagger.\n\n* Weekly Patch 42: Reboot\n** Updating SFX for Bronze Automaton summoning an Orb.\n\n* Weekly Patch 41: Chill\n** Adding SFX for Automaton's Orb spawn.\n\n* Weekly Patch 36: Power Through\n** Moving Bronze Automaton and its orbs 50px left so the rightmost orb's powers aren't cut off.\n\n* Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks\n** Bronze Automaton combat now has enemies correctly attacking from left to right.\n** Eviscerate card now has correct cost when returned from Stasis power.\n\n* Weekly Patch 15: Surprise Patch\n** Fix for Bronze Orb AI getting stuck in an incorrect state.\n\n* Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead\n** Fixed crash when Bronze Orbs' Stasis was used when your draw/discard pile was empty.\n\n* Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things\n** Bronze Automaton's Hyper Beam damage is increased from 40 -> 45.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Minions]]\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"2501":{"pageid":2501,"ns":0,"title":"Byrd","revisions":[{"revid":56923,"parentid":55677,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Byrd\n|Image  = Byrd.png\n|HP     = 25-31\n|AscHP  = 26-33\n|Powers = {{BD|Flying}} 3 ({{Asc|17|4}})\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Flying\n|Image        = Icon Flying.png\n|Description  = Takes 50% less attack damage. Cancelled if dealt attack damage X times in one turn. Resets charges at the start of next turn if not fully removed.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n'''Byrd''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Byrd}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Peck\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (1\u00d75;{{Asc|2|1\u00d76}}) damage\n.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Caw\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Gains 1 {{BD|Strength}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Strength\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Swoop\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (12;{{Asc|2|14}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stunned\n|Intent = Stunned\n|Effect = Does nothing.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Headbutt\n|Intent = Attack1\n|Effect = Deals 3 damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Go Airborne\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|17|4}}) {{BD|Flying}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Flying\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nByrd never starts with {{Int|Byrd|Swoop}}. While it has {{BD|Flying}}, Byrd will use one of the following actions each turn:\n* {{Int|Byrd|Peck}} (50% chance)\n* {{Int|Byrd|Caw}} (30% chance)\n* {{Int|Byrd|Swoop}} (20% chance)\nByrd cannot use {{Int|Byrd|Caw}} and {{Int|Byrd|Swoop}} twice in a row, or {{Int|Byrd|Peck}} three times in a row.\n\n=== Pattern While Grounded [[File:ByrdGrounded.png|80px|frameless]] ===\nIf Byrd does not have {{BD|Flying}}, it will use the following actions in order before returning to its regular pattern:\n#{{Int|Byrd|Stunned}} (replaces current [[Intent]] when {{BD|Flying}} is lost)\n#{{Int|Byrd|Headbutt}}\n#{{Int|Byrd|Go Airborne}}\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs an easy pool encounter alongside:\n* 2 other '''Byrds'''\n\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Chosen}}\n\n== Tips ==\n* Indirect damage bypasses {{BD|Flying}}. This includes damage from [[Orbs]], {{BD|Poison}}, and many other [[Debuffs]]/[[Buffs]].\n\n* Using {{C|Vault}} does not reset {{BD|Flying}}'s counter.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Byrds appear in the [[Card]] art for {{C|Chill}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 45: Impatience\n** Flight's power description now correctly resets at the start of turn.\n\n* Weekly Patch 42: Reboot\n** Adding SFX for Byrd peck attack.\n** Updating SFX for Flight and Focus Powers.\n\n* Weekly Patch 41: Chill\n** Added additional SFX for Byrd's peck attack.\n** Adding SFX for Byrd cawing.\n\n* Weekly Patch 40: Forethought\n** Adding SFX for Time Warp, Flight, Constricted, and Entangle Powers.\n\n* Weekly Patch 19: Seed\n** Fixed the turn order for Chosen + Byrd encounter. Chosen no longer applies Vulnerable before Byrd attacks.\n\n* Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!\n** Flame Barrier, Flight, Malleable, and Torii now have more checks to ensure that their effects trigger correctly.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3050":{"pageid":3050,"ns":0,"title":"Darkling","revisions":[{"revid":56958,"parentid":55725,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Darkling\n|Image  = Darkling.png\n|HP     = 48-56\n|AscHP  = 50-59\n|Powers = {{BD|Life Link}}\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}} \n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Life Link\n|Image        = Icon LifeLink.png\n|Description  = If other {{M|Darkling|Darklings}} are still alive, revives in 2 turns.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Does not stack\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\nDarkling is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Darkling}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Harden\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = Gains 12 {{KW|Block}}(.; and {{Asc|17|2}} {{BD|Strength}}.)\n|GivesToEnemy = Block, Strength\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Nip\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals N damage. N = Number between (7-11;{{Asc|2|9-13}}), chosen at the start of combat.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Chomp\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (8\u00d72;{{Asc|2|9\u00d72}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Regrowing...\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Does nothing.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Reincarnate\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Revives with 50% HP.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nOn turn one all Darklings have a 50/50 chance of using either {{Int|Darkling|Nip}} or {{Int|Darkling|Harden}}. The middle Darkling continues this pattern but cannot use {{Int|Darkling|Chomp}}.\n\n'''The outer two Darklings on all other turns:'''\n* {{Int|Darkling|Nip}} 30% chance\n* {{Int|Darkling|Chomp}} 40% chance\n* {{Int|Darkling|Harden}} 30% chance\n\nNeither {{Int|Darkling|Harden}} nor {{Int|Darkling|Chomp}} can be used twice in a row. {{Int|Darkling|Nip}} cannot be used three times in a row.\n\nAfter its HP reaches 0, its current intent changes to {{Int|Darkling|Regrowing...}} and cannot be targeted. On the next turn it will use {{Int|Darkling|Reincarnate}}.\n\n== Found With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Two other Darklings\n\n== Notes ==\n* Cards with the {{KW|Fatal}} modifier only activate their effects whenever the last Darkling is killed.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Darklings appear in the artwork of {{C|Wallop}} and {{C|Lesson Learned}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2582":{"pageid":2582,"ns":0,"title":"Giant Head","revisions":[{"revid":55616,"parentid":53428,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Giant Head\n|Image  = GiantHead.png\n|HP     = 500\n|AscHP  = 520\n|Powers = {{BD|Slow}}\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Elite\n}} {{Power Infobox|Slow}}\nGiant Head is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Giant Head}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Count\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals 13 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Glare\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = It Is Time\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (30;{{Asc|3|40}}) damage, increased by 5 for each time {{Int|Giant Head|It Is Time}} has been used this combat up to a maximum of (60;{{Asc|3|70}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nFor the first 4 ({{Asc|18|3}}) turns, it has a 50/50 chance to use either {{Int|Giant Head|Count}} or {{Int|Giant Head|Glare}}. Cannot use either move three times in a row.\n\nAfterwards, it repeats {{Int|Giant Head|It Is Time}} for the rest of combat.\n\n== Found With ==\n\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Solo\n\n== Dialogue ==\n\nAs it counts down to using {{Int|Giant Head|It Is Time}}:\n<blockquote>\n<i>{{TS|ironclad|up|4..}}</i>\n<br>\n<i>{{TS|ironclad|up|3..}}</i>  (Starts here on {{Asc|18|Ascension}})\n<br>\n<i>{{TS|ironclad|up|2..}}</i>\n<br>\n<i>{{TS|ironclad|up|1..}}</i>\n<br>\n</blockquote>\n\nAfter counting down it will say one of these lines each turn:\n<blockquote>\n<i>{{TS||up|Tick Tock Tick Tock}}</i>\n<br>\n<i>{{TS||up|Good Bye}}</i>\n<br>\n<i>{{TS||up|Why are you still here?}}</i>\n<br>\n<i>{{TS||up|It is time}}</i>\n<br>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2516":{"pageid":2516,"ns":0,"title":"Gremlin Leader","revisions":[{"revid":55806,"parentid":53476,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Ambox\n| title = WARNING!\n| color = red\n| icon = GremlinNob.png\n| message = ''This page is under construction. Information may be wrong or incomplete.''\n}}\n\n\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Gremlin Leader\n|Image  = GremlinLeader.png\n|HP     = 140-148\n|AscHP  = 145-155\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Elite\n}}\n'''Gremlin Leader''' is an [[Elite]] Enemy encountered exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Gremlin Leader}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Encourage\n|Intent = DefendBuff\n|Effect = All enemies gain (3;{{Asc|3|4}} ; {{Asc|18|5}}) {{BD|Strength}}. Other enemies gain (6;{{Asc|18|10}}) {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stab\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals 6\u00d73 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Rally!\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Summon 2 random [[Gremlins]].}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nDepending on the amount of enemies in battle, '''Gremlin Leader''' will use one of the following actions each turn:\n==== With 0 Gremlins ====\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Rally!}} (75% chance)\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Stab}} (25% chance)\n\n==== With 1 Gremlin ====\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Rally!}} (50% chance)*\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Stab}} (50% chance)*\n:<nowiki>* </nowiki> ''If last used action was'' {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Encourage}}\nor\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Rally!}} (62.5% chance)**\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Encourage}} (37.5% chance)**\n:<nowiki>** </nowiki> ''If last used action was'' {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Stab}}\n\n==== With 2 or more Gremlins ====\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Encourage}} (66% chance)\n* {{Int|Gremlin Leader|Stab}} (34% chance)\n'''Gremlin Leader''' cannot use any [[Intent|intent]] twice in a row. No more than 3 small [[Gremlins]] can be present at once.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs an [[Elite]] encounter alongside:\n* 2 random [[Gremlins]]\n\n== Tips ==\n\n== Trivia ==\n* '''Gremlin Leader''' is female, as stated by a developer.<ref>[https://www.reddit.com/r/slaythespire/comments/duo993/comment/f77ja14/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web2x Reddit]</ref>\n\n== References ==\n<references />\n\n== Update History ==\n* Patch V1.1: The Dealer\n** Fixed enemy order issues in Slime Boss, Gremlin Leader, and Reptomancer encounters.\n\n* Weekly Patch 37: Darkness\n** Gremlin Leader HP lowered. 155 - 164 -> 140 - 148. Asc: 162 - 172 -> 145 - 155.\n\n* Weekly Patch 33: Terror\n** Gremlin Leader summon used the incorrect RNG, resulting in different enemies for the same seed.\n\n* Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning\n** Gremlin Leader's minion summon is now seeded.\n\n* Weekly Patch 14: Bullet Time\n** New animations for the Gremlin Leader.\n** In Fast Mode, Gremlin Leader's minions spawn a lot faster.\n\n* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!\n** Little gremlins no longer yell about escaping if they're dead. Corpses don't yell.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"1792":{"pageid":1792,"ns":0,"title":"Gremlin Nob","revisions":[{"revid":56364,"parentid":55807,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n| Name   = Gremlin Nob\n| Image  = GremlinNob.png\n| HP     = 82-86\n| AscHP  = 85-90\n| Debut  = Act 1\n| Type   = Elite\n}} \n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Enrage\n| Image        = Icon Anger.png\n| Description  = Whenever you play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card, gains X {{BD|Strength}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToEnemy = Strength\n}}\n'''Gremlin Nob''' is an [[Elite]] found in [[Act 1]] and in the [[Act 2]] event {{E|The Colosseum}}.\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Gremlin Nob}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Bellow\n| Intent = Buff\n| Effect = Gains (2;{{Asc|18|3}}) {{BD|Enrage}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Enrage\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Skull Bash\n| Intent = DebuffAttack2\n| Effect = Deals (6;{{Asc|3|8}}) damage. Applies 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Bull Rush\n| Intent = Attack3\n| Effect = Deals (14;{{Asc|3|16}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways starts with {{Int|Gremlin Nob|Bellow}} then has a 33% chance of using {{Int|Gremlin Nob|Skull Bash}} and a 67% chance of using {{Int|Gremlin Nob|Bull Rush}}. Cannot use {{Int|Gremlin Nob|Bull Rush}} three times in a row.\n\nAt {{Asc|18|Ascension}}, '''Gremlin Nob''' uses {{Int|Gremlin Nob|Skull Bash}} on the 2nd turn and uses {{Int|Gremlin Nob|Bull Rush}} twice afterwards, then repeats this pattern for the rest of the fight.\n\n== In Party With ==\n\n=== Act 1 ===\nAs an [[Elite]]:\n\n* Solo\n\n=== Act 2 ===\nIn the {{E|The Colosseum}} event, when {{Frame|Victory}} is chosen, alongside:\n\n* 1 {{M|Taskmaster}}\n\n== Tips ==\nThe player is heavily encouraged to not play {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} after '''Turn 1''' of this fight, and to try to end this fight by '''Turn 3''', however, some cards like {{C|Glacier}} and {{C|Leg Sweep}} tend to still be very positive if a '''Turn 3''' kill is no longer possible.\n\n== Update History ==\n\n* '''Slay the Spire 1.0: Farewell Early Access'''\n** Colosseum Nob fight ordering swapped so that the Nob can apply Vulnerable.\n* '''Weekly Patch 56: The Collector'''\n** Colosseum event's second fight is now a Gremlin Nob + Taskmaster (rather than 2 Gremlin Nobs)\n* '''Weekly Patch 41'''\n** Colosseum Nobs no longer play double music.\n** Killing a Colosseum Nob no longer causes the music to stop.\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Gremlin Nob gets a minor nerf.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2326":{"pageid":2326,"ns":0,"title":"Hexaghost","revisions":[{"revid":55819,"parentid":51683,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Hexaghost\n|Image  = Hexaghost.png\n|Icon   = Map-Hexaghost.png\n|HP     = 250\n|AscHP  = 264\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Boss\n}} {{M|Hexaghost}} is a [[Boss]] that can appear at the end of [[Act 1]] or the [[Act 3]] event {{E|Mind Bloom}}.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Hexaghost}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Activate\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Does nothing.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Divider\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (N+1)\u00d76 damage. N = Player's HP at the start of the turn, divided by 12 (rounded down).}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Sear\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals 6 damage. Adds (1;{{Asc|19|2}}) {{C|Burn|Burns}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (5\u00d72;{{Asc|4|6\u00d72}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Inflame\n|Intent = DefendBuff\n|Effect = Gains 12 {{KW|Block}} and (2;{{Asc|19|3}}) {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Inferno\n|Intent = DebuffAttack5\n|Effect = Deals (2\u00d76;{{Asc|4|3\u00d76}}) damage. Adds 3 {{C|Burn|Burns+}} into your discard pile. Upgrades all {{C|Burn|Burns}}. For the rest of combat, any {{C|Burn}} created by {{Int|Hexaghost|Sear}} will be upgraded.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nAlways starts with {{Int|Hexaghost|Activate}} followed by {{Int|Hexaghost|Divider}}.\nFor the rest of combat, repeats the following pattern:\n# {{Int|Hexaghost|Sear}}\n# {{Int|Hexaghost|Tackle}}\n# {{Int|Hexaghost|Sear}}\n# {{Int|Hexaghost|Inflame}}\n# {{Int|Hexaghost|Tackle}}\n# {{Int|Hexaghost|Sear}}\n# {{Int|Hexaghost|Inferno}}\n\n== Hints ==\n* This fight is a race to kill Hexaghost before turn 9. Before that, Hexaghost isn't very threatening, prefering to fire low damage {{Int|Hexaghost|Sear|Sears}} and {{Int|Hexaghost|Tackle|Tackles}}. However, on the 9th turn, it will use {{Int|Hexaghost|Inferno}}, which deals 24 ({{Asc|4|30}}, {{Asc|19|36}}) damage and fills your discard pile with {{C|Burn|Burns+}}. It's very hard to survive this attack, let alone the turns after.\n** To kill Hexaghost in 9 turns, on average you need to deal around 30 damage per turn. Achieving this requires some sort of scaling, such as {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n* On the 2nd turn, Hexaghost uses {{Int|Hexaghost|Divider}}, the only attack in the game that scales with your current HP. If you are already low on health, this attack deals pitiful damage. Therefore, it's often preferable to '''not''' rest before this fight, and instead upgrade a card that will help you beat Hexaghost before {{Int|Hexaghost|Inferno}}.\n** For example, if you have between 12 and 23 HP, {{Int|Hexaghost|Divider}} deals only 12 damage, easily blocked.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Hexaghost appears in the artwork of {{C|Grand Finale}} and {{C|Compile Driver}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"1737":{"pageid":1737,"ns":0,"title":"Jaw Worm","revisions":[{"revid":56360,"parentid":55832,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n| Name   = Jaw Worm\n| Image  = JawWorm.png\n| HP     = 40-44\n| AscHP  = 42-46\n| Debut  = Act 1\n| Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Enemy Infobox\n| Name   = Jaw Worm (Hard)\n| Image  = JawWorm.png\n| HP     = 40-44\n| AscHP  = 42-46\n| Powers = {{BD|Strength}} 3 ({{Asc|2|4}}/{{Asc|17|5}})<br> {{BD|Block}}  6 ({{Asc|17|9}})\n| Debut  = Act 3\n| Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Jaw Worm''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that can show up in Act 1, and has a hard variant that can show up in Act 3.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Jaw Worm}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Chomp\n| Intent = Attack3\n| Effect = Deals (11;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Bellow\n| Intent = DefendBuff\n| Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|2|4}} ; {{Asc|17|5}}) {{BD|Strength}}. Gains (6;{{Asc|17|9}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Strength, Block\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Thrash\n| Intent = DefendAttack2\n| Effect = Deals 7 damage. Gains 5 {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways starts with {{Int|Jaw Worm|Chomp}}. If it is found in Act 3, it starts with the effects of {{Int|Jaw Worm|Bellow}}, and for its first action it has a 45% chance of starting with {{Int|Jaw Worm|Bellow}}, a 30% chance of {{Int|Jaw Worm|Thrash}} and a 25% chance of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Chomp}}\n* After using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Chomp}}, it has a 59% chance of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Bellow}} and a 41% of {{Int|Jaw Worm|Thrash}}\n* After using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Bellow}}, it has a 56% chance of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Thrash}} and a 44% of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Chomp}}\n* After using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Thrash}}, it has a 45% chance of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Bellow}}, a 30% chance of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Thrash}} and a 25% chance of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Chomp}}. Unless {{Int|Jaw Worm|Thrash}} has been used 2 turns in a row, then it has a 64% chance of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Bellow}}, and a 36% of using {{Int|Jaw Worm|Chomp}}\n\n== In Party With ==\n\n=== Act 1 ===\nAs an easy pool encounter:\n\n* Solo\n\nAs half of an Exodium Wildlife encounter in the hard pool:\n\n* 1 {{M|Red Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Green Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}\n* 1 {{M|Acid Slime (M)}}\n\n=== Act 3 ===\nIn the Jaw Worm Horde encounter, it appears along with 2 other Jaw Worm's, all 3 are the Hard variant.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Jaw Worm appears in the artwork of {{C|Reaper}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2211":{"pageid":2211,"ns":0,"title":"Louses","revisions":[{"revid":55804,"parentid":53440,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"== Red Louse ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Red Louse\n|Image  = RedLouse.png\n|HP     = 10-15\n|AscHP  = 11-16\n|Powers = {{BD|Curl Up}} N, where N is random between 3-7 ({{Asc|7|4-8}} {{!}} {{Asc|17|9-12}})\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Curl Up}}\nThe '''Red Louse''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Red Louse}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Bite\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals N damage. N = Number between (5-7;{{Asc|2|6-8}}), chosen at the start of combat.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Grow\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|17|4}}) {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nHas a 25% chance to use {{Int|Red Louse|Grow}} and a 75% chance of using {{Int|Red Louse|Bite}}. It cannot use the same move three times in a row.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}} it cannot use {{Int|Red Louse|Grow}} any more than twice in a row.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nIn the Easy Pool along with:\n\n* '''Red''' or '''Green Louse'''\n* 2 '''Red''' or '''Green Louses'''\n* {{M|Cultist}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\nIn the Hard Pool with:\n\n* 2 '''Red''' or '''Green Louses'''\n\nCan be found as half of the '''Exordium Thugs''' encounter along with either:\n\n* One of the [[Slavers]]\n* One {{M|Cultist}}\n* One {{M|Looter}}\nCan be found as half of the '''Exordium Wildlife''' encounter with either:\n\n* {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\n== Green Louse ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Green Louse\n|Image  = GreenLouse.png\n|HP     = 11-17\n|AscHP  = 12-18\n|Powers = {{BD|Curl Up}} N, where N is random between 3-7 ({{Asc|7|4-8}} {{!}} {{Asc|17|9-12}})\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Curl Up}}\nThe '''Green Louse''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Green Louse}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Bite\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals N damage. N = Number between (5-7;{{Asc|2|6-8}}), chosen at the start of combat.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Spit Web\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 2 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nHas a 25% chance to use {{Int|Green Louse|Spit Web}} and a 75% chance of using {{Int|Green Louse|Bite}}. It cannot use the same move three times in a row.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}} it cannot use {{Int|Green Louse|Spit Web}} any more than twice in a row.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nIn the Easy Pool along with:\n\n* '''Red''' or '''Green Louse'''\n* 2 '''Red''' or '''Green Louses'''\n* {{M|Cultist}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\nIn the Hard Pool with:\n\n* 2 '''Red''' or '''Green Louses'''\n\nCan be found as half of the '''Exordium Thugs''' encounter along with either:\n\n* One of the [[Slavers]]\n* One {{M|Cultist}}\n* One {{M|Looter}}\nCan be found as half of the '''Exordium Wildlife''' encounter with either:\n\n* {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Red Louse appear in the artwork of {{C|Carnage}}, {{C|Reaper}}, {{C|Skewer}}, {{C|Grand Finale}}, {{C|Reach Heaven}}, {{C|Smite}} and {{C|Through Violence}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2388":{"pageid":2388,"ns":0,"title":"Sentry","revisions":[{"revid":53452,"parentid":37785,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Sentry\n|Image  = Sentry.png\n|HP     = 38-42\n|AscHP  = 39-45\n|Powers = {{BD|Artifact}} 1\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Elite\n}}{{Power Infobox|Artifact}}{{Small Card Infobox|Dazed}}\n'''Sentry''' is an [[Elite]] found in [[Act 1]] in groups of three. In [[Act 2]], a Sentry can be fought as a common [[Slay the Spire Wiki/Enemies|Enemy]].\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Sentry}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Bolt\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Adds (2;{{Asc|18|3}}) {{C|Dazed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Beam\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (9;{{Asc|3|10}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nUses {{Int|Sentry|Bolt}} followed by {{Int|Sentry|Beam}}, repeating for the rest of the combat.\n\nIn the Elite encounter, the middle '''Sentry''' instead uses {{Int|Sentry|Beam}} followed by {{Int|Sentry|Bolt}}.\n\n== In Party With ==\n\n=== Act 1 ===\nAs an [[Elite]] alongside:\n\n* 2 other '''Sentries'''\n\n=== Act 2 ===\nIn the hard pool alongside:\n\n* 1 {{M|Spheric Guardian}}\n\n== Hints ==\n* During the Elite encounter, you should focus in eliminating the 1st or the 3rd '''Sentry''' as fast as possible, ignoring the 2nd one. This prevents you from taking 18 ({{Asc|3|20}}) damage each other turn, making the rest of the fight much easier.\n\n* The {{C|Dazed}} in your discard pile won't hamper you as long as you have cards remaining in your draw pile. Once you run out of cards, they will be shuffled into your draw pile and massively reduce your ability to draw playable cards. It is important to kill at least one of the Sentries ''before'' you shuffle your draw pile, as you may no longer have the ability to deal with all '''Sentries''' at the same time once the {{C|Dazed}} come in.\n\n* {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Evolve}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}} and {{C|Fire Breathing}} convert {{C|Dazed}} into advantage.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Sentry appears in the artwork of {{C|Searing Blow}}, {{C|Reaper}}, {{C|Predator}}, {{C|Reflex}}, {{C|Malaise}}, {{C|Fear No Evil}} and {{C|Rushdown}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2435":{"pageid":2435,"ns":0,"title":"Shelled Parasite","revisions":[{"revid":55630,"parentid":53457,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Shelled Parasite\n|Image  = ShelledParasite.png\n|HP     = 68-72\n|AscHP  = 70-75\n|Powers = {{BD|Plated Armor}} 14\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}} {{Power Infobox|Plated Armor}}\n'''Shelled Parasite''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Shelled Parasite}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Double Strike\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (6\u00d72;{{Asc|2|7\u00d72}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Life Suck\n|Intent = BuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage. Heals HP equal to unblocked damage dealt.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Fell\n|Intent = DebuffAttack4\n|Effect = Deals (18;{{Asc|2|21}}) damage. Applies 2 {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stunned\n|Intent = Stunned\n|Effect = Does nothing.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Shelled Parasite''' cannot use {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Fell}} on its first turn. After that, it will use one of the following attacks each turn:\n* {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Double Strike}} (40% chance)\n* {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Life Suck}} (40% chance)\n* {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Fell}} (20% chance)\n'''Shelled Parasite''' cannot use {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Double Strike}} or {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Life Suck}} three times in a row, or {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Fell}} twice in a row. \n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, '''Shelled Parasite''' will always start with {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Fell}}.\n\nIf all of its {{BD|Plated Armor}} is broken, '''Shelled Parasite''' will change its current [[Intent]] to {{Int|Shelled Parasite|Stunned}}. This can only happen once per combat.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs an easy pool encounter:\n* Solo\n\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* '''Shelled Parasite''' appears in the [[Card]] art for {{C|Barrage}} and {{C|Talk to the Hand}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n\n* Patch V1.1: The Dealer\n** Improved lifesteal logic for Reaper and Shelled Parasite.\n\n* Weekly Patch 38: Bane\n** Parasite + Fungi Beast combat can actually be encountered now.\n\n* Weekly Patch 37: Darkness\n** New City Encounter - Shelled Parasite and Fungi Beast.\n** Shelled Parasite and Slaver combined combat has been removed from The City.\n\n* Weekly Patch 35: Aggregate\n** Shelled Parasite now accounts for Buffer and Intangible with its life leech action.\n\n* Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life\n** We updated the animations for several monsters! Affected monsters include: Shelled Parasite\n\n* Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things\n** Slaver and Shelled Parasite combat in the city have their order swapped so the slaver will not apply Vulnerable before attacked by Parasite.\n\n* Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!\n** Raising the Slaver's position a bit for Slaver + Parasite combat (power hidden by card).\n\n* Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance\n** Shelled Parasite enemy buff.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2398":{"pageid":2398,"ns":0,"title":"Slavers","revisions":[{"revid":55660,"parentid":53443,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"= Blue Slaver =\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Blue Slaver\n|Image  = SlaverBlue.png\n|HP     = 46-50\n|AscHP  = 48-52\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Blue Slaver''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found in Act 1 and Act 2. They can also appear in [[Elite]] combats and {{E|The Colosseum}} [[Event]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Blue Slaver}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stab\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (12;{{Asc|2|13}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Rake\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (7;{{Asc|2|8}}) damage. Applies (1;{{Asc|17|2}}) {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nEach turn, '''Blue Slaver''' has a 60% chance to use {{Int|Blue Slaver|Stab}} and a 40% chance to use {{Int|Blue Slaver|Rake}}. The same attack cannot be used three times in a row.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, '''Blue Slaver''' will never use {{Int|Blue Slaver|Rake}} twice in a row.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 1 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter:\n* Solo\nIn the Exordium Thugs encounter along with either:\n* 1 {{M|Green Louse}} or {{M|Red Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Acid Slime (M)}} or {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs an [[Elite]] encounter along with:\n* 1 {{M|Taskmaster}}\n* 1 {{M|Red Slaver}}\nIn the first fight of {{E|The Colosseum}} [[Event]] alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Red Slaver}}\n\n= Red Slaver =\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Red Slaver\n|Image  = SlaverRed.png\n|HP     = 46-50\n|AscHP  = 48-52\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Entangled}}\n'''Red Slaver''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found in Act 1 and Act 2. They can also appear in [[Elite]] combats and {{E|The Colosseum}} [[Event]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Red Slaver}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stab\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (13;{{Asc|2|14}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Scrape\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (8;{{Asc|2|9}}) damage. Applies (1;{{Asc|17|2}}) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Entangle\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Entangled}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n'''Red Slaver''' will always start the battle with {{Int|Red Slaver|Stab}}. If '''Red Slaver''' has not used {{Int|Red Slaver|Entangle}} yet, it has a 25% chance to be used each turn. '''Red Slaver''' will repeat the pattern of {{Int|Red Slaver|Scrape}}, {{Int|Red Slaver|Scrape}}, {{Int|Red Slaver|Stab}} until {{Int|Red Slaver|Entangle}} is used. After using {{Int|Red Slaver|Entangle}}, '''Red Slaver''' has a 55% chance of using {{Int|Red Slaver|Stab}} and a 45% chance of using {{Int|Red Slaver|Scrape}}. '''Red Slaver''' cannot use the same attack three times in a row, and can only use {{Int|Red Slaver|Entangle}} once per combat.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, '''Red Slaver''' will repeat the pattern of {{Int|Red Slaver|Scrape}}, {{Int|Red Slaver|Stab}} until {{Int|Red Slaver|Entangle}} is used. After {{Int|Red Slaver|Entangle}} is used, '''Red Slaver''' cannot use {{Int|Red Slaver|Scrape}} twice in a row.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 1 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter:\n* Solo\nIn the Exordium Thugs encounter along with either:\n* 1 {{M|Green Louse}} or {{M|Red Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Acid Slime (M)}} or {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs an [[Elite]] encounter along with:\n* 1 {{M|Taskmaster}}\n* 1 {{M|Blue Slaver}}\nIn the first fight of {{E|The Colosseum}} [[Event]] alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Blue Slaver}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The Red Slaver is the only thing in the game that can apply {{BD|Entangled}}.\n* Blue Slaver appears in the artwork of {{C|Blood for Blood}}, {{C|Disarm}}, {{C|Rampage}}, {{C|Outmaneuver}}, {{C|Sneaky Strike}} and {{C|Choke}}.\n* Red Slaver appears in the artwork of {{C|Headbutt}} and {{C|Rampage}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 53: Blizzard\n** Adding a VFX for Entangle by Red Slaver (NON-Fast Mode only)\n\n* Weekly Patch 42: Reboot\n** Updating SFX for Entangle Power.\n\n* Weekly Patch 40: Forethought\n** Adding SFX for Time Warp, Flight, Constricted, and Entangle Powers.\n\n* Weekly Patch 37: Darkness\n** Shelled Parasite and Slaver combined combat has been removed from The City.\n\n* Weekly Patch 36: Power Through\n** Slaver/Looter and Slaver/Monster encounters in Act 1 swap positions to prevent Vulnerable + Attack turns.\n\n* Weekly Patch 22: Testing the Third Character\n** Some redundant code on the red slaver removed for slight performance increase.\n\n* Weekly Patch 12: Lunar New Year\n** The Blue Slaver enemy can no longer be fought as one of the first 3 monsters in Act 1.\n\n* Weekly Patch 11: A Library of Features\n** Fixed issue where incorrect intent damage was shown for Red Slaver.\n\n* Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things\n** Slaver and Shelled Parasite combat in the city have their order swapped so the slaver will not apply Vulnerable before attacked by Parasite.\n\n* Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!\n** Red Slaver's AI is updated to not apply Vulnerable on turn 1.\n** Raising the Slaver's position a bit for Slaver + Parasite combat (power hidden by card).\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"1782":{"pageid":1782,"ns":0,"title":"Slime Boss","revisions":[{"revid":55944,"parentid":51678,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Slime Boss\n|Image  = SlimeBoss.png\n|Icon   = Map-SlimeBoss.png\n|HP     = 140\n|AscHP  = 150\n|Powers = {{BD|Split}}\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Boss\n}} {{Power Infobox|Split}}{{Small Card Infobox|Slimed}}\n'''Slime Boss''' is a [[Boss]] that can appear at the end of [[Act 1]] or the [[Act 3]] event {{E|Mind Bloom}}.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Slime Boss}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Goop Spray\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Adds (3;{{Asc|19|5}}) {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Preparing\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Does nothing.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Slam\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (35;{{Asc|4|38}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Split\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Disappears and spawns 1 {{M|Acid Slime (L)}} and 1 {{M|Spike Slime (L)}} with its current HP.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nRepeats the following pattern:\n#{{Int|Slime Boss|Goop Spray}}\n#{{Int|Slime Boss|Preparing}}\n#{{Int|Slime Boss|Slam}}\n\nOnce its HP reaches 50% or lower, its current [[Intent]] will be immediately changed to {{Int|Slime Boss|Split}}.\n\n== Hints ==\n* Until '''Slime Boss''' {{Int|Slime Boss|Split|splits}}, {{Int|Slime Boss|Slam}} is the only way it can harm you. Other than this attack, it spends most of the fight doing nothing. There are many ways to deal with it other than with {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Weak}}:\n** As long as you can deal 70 ({{Asc|9|75}}) damage by turn 3, you can force '''Slime Boss''' to {{Int|Slime Boss|Split|split}} before it attacks.\n** You may fully negate {{Int|Slime Boss|Slam}} with {{C|Buffer}}, {{R|Fossilized Helix}}, {{R|Incense Burner}} and {{P|Ghost in a Jar}}.\n** Rest before the fight to have more than 35 ({{Asc|4|38}}) HP, then simply tank it. After all, you always heal after boss fights.\n* {{Int|Slime Boss|Split}} creates two [[Slimes|Large Slimes]] with '''Slime Boss'''' remaining HP. Thus it's better to cause '''Slime Boss''' to lose as much health as possible before the {{Int|Slime Boss|Split|splitting}}.\n** This can be done by bringing the boss as close as possible to half HP, then applying {{BD|Vulnerable}} and spending as much energy as possible playing Attacks.\n** With {{KW|Wrath}}, the [[Watcher]] is particularly good at killing or nearly killing '''Slime Boss''' before it can {{Int|Slime Boss|Split|split}}.\n* '''Slime Boss''' and its [[Slimes]] will clog your Deck with {{C|Slimed}} the longer the fight goes on, particularly harshly on higher [[Ascension|ascensions]].\n** {{C|Evolve}} and {{C|Fire Breathing}} turn those {{C|Slimed}} into advantage.\n* Sources of AOE damage like {{C|Whirlwind}} are effective against the [[Slimes]] that spawn after '''Slime Boss''' {{Int|Slime Boss|Split|Splits}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* '''Slime Boss''' appears in the artwork of {{C|Evolve}} and {{C|Grand Finale}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"2249":{"pageid":2249,"ns":0,"title":"Slimes","revisions":[{"revid":55614,"parentid":53423,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{TOC limit|2}}\n== Spike Slime (L) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spike Slime (L)\n|Image  = SpikeSlimeL.png\n|HP     = 64-70\n|AscHP  = 67-73\n|Powers = {{BD|Split}}\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Split}}\n'''Spike Slime (L)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spike Slime (L)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies (2;{{Asc|17|3}}) {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Flame Tackle\n|Intent = DebuffAttack4\n|Effect = Deals (16;{{Asc|2|18}}) damage. Adds 2 {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Split\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Disappears and spawns 2 {{M|Spike Slime (M)|Spike Slimes (M)}} with its current HP.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nHas a 30% chance of using {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Flame Tackle}} and a 70% chance of using {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Lick}}. Cannot use the same move three times in a row.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, it cannot use {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Lick}} twice in a row.\n\nOnce its HP reaches 50% or lower, its current [[Intent]] will be interrupted and changed to {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\n=== Found With ===\nIt is only found by itself in combat.\n\n== Spike Slime (M) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spike Slime (M)\n|Image  = SpikeSlimeM.png\n|HP     = 28-32\n|AscHP  = 29-34\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Spike Slime (M)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spike Slime (M)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Flame Tackle\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (8;{{Asc|2|10}}) damage. Adds a {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nIdentical to {{M|Spike Slime (L)}} but it cannot {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with an {{M|Acid Slime (S)}}.\n\nCan be a part of the '''Exordium Thugs''' encounter along with either:\n\n* One of the [[Slavers]]\n* {{M|Cultist}}\n* {{M|Looter}}\n\nCan be a part of the '''Exordium Wildlife''' encounter along with either:\n\n* {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\n== Spike Slime (S) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spike Slime (S)\n|Image  = SpikeSlimeS.png\n|HP     = 10-14\n|AscHP  = 11-15\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Spike Slime (S)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that is exclusively found in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spike Slime (S)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (5;{{Asc|2|6}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with an {{M|Acid Slime (M)}}.\n\nIn the '''Lots of Slimes''' encounter with:\n\n* Two other {{M|Spike Slime (S)|Spike Slimes (S)}}\n* Two {{M|Acid Slime (S)|Small Acid Slimes}}\n\n== Acid Slime (L) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Acid Slime (L)\n|Image  = AcidSlimeL.png\n|HP     = 65-69\n|AscHP  = 68-72\n|Powers = {{BD|Split}}\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}{{Power Infobox|Split}}\n'''Acid Slime (L)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] exclusively found in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Acid Slime (L)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Corrosive Spit\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (11;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage. Adds 2 {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 2 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (16;{{Asc|2|18}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Split\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Disappears and spawns 2 {{M|Acid Slime (M)|Acid Slimes (M)}} with its current HP.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nHas a 30% ({{Asc|17|40%}}) chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Corrosive Spit}}, a 40% ({{Asc|17|30%}}) chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Tackle}} and a 30% chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Lick}} every turn.\n\nCannot use {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Tackle}} ({{Asc|17|Lick}}) twice in a row and cannot use other moves three times in a row.\n\nOnce its HP reaches 50% or lower, its current [[Intent]] will be interrupted and changed to {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nOnly found solo.\n\n== Acid Slime (M) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Acid Slime (M)\n|Image  = AcidSlimeM.png\n|HP     = 28-32\n|AscHP  = 29-34\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Acid Slime (M)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Acid Slime (M)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Corrosive Spit\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (7;{{Asc|2|8}}) damage. Adds a {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nIdentical pattern to {{M|Acid Slime (L)}} but it cannot {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}: Every turn it has a 40% change of using {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Corrosive Spit}}, a 40% chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Tackle}}, and a 20% chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Lick}}. {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Lick}} cannot be used twice in a row and other moves cannot be used 3 times in a row.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with a {{M|Spike Slime (S)}}.\n\nCan be a part of the '''Exordium Thugs''' encounter along with either:\n* One of the [[Slavers]]\n* {{M|Cultist}}\n* {{M|Looter}}\nCan be found as half of the '''Exordium Wildlife''' encounter with either:\n\n* {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\n== Acid Slime (S) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Acid Slime (S)\n|Image  = AcidSlimeS.png\n|HP     = 8-12\n|AscHP  = 9-13\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Acid Slime (S)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that is exclusively found in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Acid Slime (S)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack1\n|Effect = Deals (3;{{Asc|2|4}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with a {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}.\n\nIn the '''Lots of Slimes''' encounter with:\n\n* One other {{M|Acid Slime (S)}}\n* Three {{M|Spike Slime (S)|Small Spike Slimes}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Acid Slimes appear in the artwork of {{C|Evolve}}, {{C|Intimidate}}, {{C|Nightmare}}, {{C|Consecrate}}, {{C|Halt}} and {{C|Thinking Ahead}}.\n* Spike Slimes appear in the artwork of {{C|Carnage}}, {{C|Reaper}}, {{C|Grand Finale}} and {{C|Conclude}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2484":{"pageid":2484,"ns":0,"title":"Snecko","revisions":[{"revid":55947,"parentid":53468,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Ambox\n| title = WARNING!\n| color = red\n| icon = GremlinNob.png\n| message = ''This page is under construction. Information may be wrong or incomplete.''\n}}\n\n\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Snecko\n|Image  = Snecko.png\n|HP     = 114-120\n|AscHP  = 120-125\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Confused}}\n'''Snecko''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Snecko}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Perplexing Glare\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies {{BD|Confused}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Bite\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (15;{{Asc|2|18}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tail Whip\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (8;{{Asc|2|10}}) damage. Applies 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}(.; and {{Asc|17|2}} {{BD|Weak}}).}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways starts with {{Int|Snecko|Perplexing Glare}}, then uses one of the following actions each turn:\n* {{Int|Snecko|Bite}} (60% chance)\n* {{Int|Snecko|Tail Whip}} (40% chance)\nSnecko will not use {{Int|Snecko|Bite}} three times in a row.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter:\n* Solo\n\n== Tips ==\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Snecko is a portmanteau of the words \"snake\" and \"gecko\".\n* The {{R|Snecko Eye}} and {{R|Snecko Skull}} [[Relics]] are references to this enemy.\n* Snecko's '''Tail Whip''' may be a reference to the ''Pok\u00e9mon'' [https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Tail_Whip_(move) move of the same name].\n* Snecko appears in the artwork of {{C|Rebound}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Patch V1.1: The Dealer\n** WobblyLine VFX used in Snecko's glare is now larger and scales correctly with resolution.\n\n* Weekly Patch 42: Reboot\n** Adding SFX for Snecko's glare.\n** Updating SFX for Confusion Power.\n\n* Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance\n** Snecko enemy buff.\n\n* Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!\n** Snecko uses a Bite VFX when it bites now.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3054":{"pageid":3054,"ns":0,"title":"Spire Growth","revisions":[{"revid":55953,"parentid":53499,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spire Growth\n|Image  = SpireGrowth.png\n|HP     = 170\n|AscHP  = 190\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Constricted}}\nSpire Growth is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Spire Growth}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Constrict\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies (10;{{Asc|2|12}}) {{BD|Constricted}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Quick Tackle\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (16;{{Asc|2|18}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Smash\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals (22;{{Asc|2|25}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nEach turn, it has a 50/50 chance to use either {{Int|Spire Growth|Quick Tackle}} or {{Int|Spire Growth|Constrict}}.\n\nIf {{Int|Spire Growth|Constrict}} was used last turn or the player already has {{BD|Constricted}}, it uses {{Int|Spire Growth|Smash}} instead.\n\nCannot use either attack three times in a row.\n\n== Found With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Solo\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2580":{"pageid":2580,"ns":0,"title":"Taskmaster","revisions":[{"revid":55971,"parentid":53484,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Taskmaster\n|Image  = Taskmaster.png\n|HP     = 54-60\n|AscHP  = 57-64\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Elite\n}}{{Small Card Infobox|Wound}}\nTaskmaster is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Taskmaster}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Scouring Whip\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals 7 damage. Adds (1 {{C|Wound}}; {{Asc|2|2}} ; {{Asc|18|3}} {{C|Wound|Wounds}}) into your discard pile. (;Gains {{Asc|18|1}} {{BD|Strength}}.)}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n== Found With ==\n\n=== Act 2 ===\nFound in the '''[[Slavers]]''' Elite encounter with:\n* {{M|Red Slaver}}\n* {{M|Blue Slaver}}\n\nFound in {{E|The Colosseum}} event alongside:\n\n* {{M|Enemy Name=|Gremlin Nob}}\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:ToUpdate]]\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"3026":{"pageid":3026,"ns":0,"title":"The Collector","revisions":[{"revid":56531,"parentid":55703,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = The Collector\n|Image  = TheCollector.png\n|Icon   = Map-Collector.png\n|HP     = 282\n|AscHP  = 300\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Boss\n}}\nThe Collector is a [[Boss]] found at the end of [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|The Collector}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Spawn\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Summons up to 2 {{M|Torch Head|Torch Heads}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Fireball\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (18;{{Asc|4|21}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Buff\n|Intent = DefendBuff\n|Effect = All enemies gain (3;{{Asc|4|4}} ; {{Asc|19|5}}) {{BD|Strength}}. Gains (15;{{Asc|9|18}} ; {{Asc|19|23}}) {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Mega Debuff\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies (3;{{Asc|19|5}}) {{BD|Weak}}, (3;{{Asc|19|5}}) {{BD|Vulnerable}} and (3;{{Asc|19|5}}) {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nAlways starts with {{Int|The Collector|Spawn}} and always uses {{Int|The Collector|Mega Debuff}} on turn 4.\n\nCan only have two {{M|Torch Head|Torch Heads}} summoned at a time.\n\n'''If there are 0-1 {{M|Torch Head|Torch Heads}} alive:'''\n* {{Int|The Collector|Spawn}} 25% chance\n* {{Int|The Collector|Fireball}} 45% chance\n* {{Int|The Collector|Buff}} 30% chance\n\n'''If both {{M|Torch Head|Torch Heads}} are alive:'''\n* {{Int|The Collector|Fireball}} 70% chance\n* {{Int|The Collector|Buff}} 30% chance\n\nShe cannot use {{Int|The Collector|Buff}} twice in a row and cannot use {{Int|The Collector|Fireball}} 3 times in a row.\n\n= Torch Head =\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Torch Head\n|Image  = TorchHead.png\n|HP     = 38-40\n|AscHP  = 40-45\n|Powers = {{BD|Minion}}\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Minion\n}}\nTorch Head is a {{BD|Minion}} spawned by the Collector.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Torch Head}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals 7 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n{{Clear}}\n== Trivia ==\n* '''The Collector''' is confirmed to be female. <ref>https://imgur.com/a/cOqF1p8 </ref>\n** This is further implied with {{M2|Queen}} in the sequel sharing many direct connections to '''The Collector'''.\n* '''The Collector''' is featured in the banner for Weekly Patch 56.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Minions]]\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]}}}}